{#
 # The signed-in user's avatar: their initials, drawn here.
 #
 # It used to be an image fetched from gravatar.com with the MD5 of the e-mail
 # address, so every page told a third party who was signed in and from which
 # IP address — for a grey silhouette, most users having no Gravatar account.
 # Nothing leaves the application any more.
 #
 # Solid ink and white rather than a tint: the same markup sits on the white
 # top bar and on the dark sidebar header of the phone layout, where a tint
 # vanished.
 #
 # Decorative: the link around it carries the accessible name.
 #}
{% set initials = ((app.user.firstName|default('')|slice(0, 1)) ~ (app.user.lastName|default('')|slice(0, 1)))|upper %}
<span class="avatar avatar-sm bg-primary text-white fw-semibold" aria-hidden="true">{{ initials ?: app.user.email|slice(0, 1)|upper }}</span>
